PXL
----

Minimal 2D graphics library in C99.

Features:
  - 2D primitives: line, rect, circle, triangle (outline + filled)
  - Canvas with scissor clipping, translation offset, color, clear, blit
  - Text rendering with mono or proportional LSB bitmask fonts, including alignment
  - Transformations: flip (horizontal, vertical) and scale for bitmasks and text during rendering
  - Backends: SDL2, X11 (uses SHM, XIM/XIC extensions for performance and UTF-8 input)
  - Keyboard/mouse input


Build:
  make                  # Build libpxl.a (default backend: x11)
  make PXL_BACKEND=sdl  # Build with SDL2 backend
  make lint             # Static analysis with strict warnings (-Werror)
  make test             # Run unit tests found in test/
  make demo             # Build demos found in demo/
  make tool             # Build tools found in tool/
  make clean            # Remove build artifacts (incl. the ones in demo, tools and test)

  Main configuration is defined in Makefile.inc. Copy 'config.mk.example' to 'config.mk' to customize
  backend, CFLAGS, or library paths.


Vendoring:
  pxl is meant to be vendored as-is: flat sources, no generated files, no
  config header (POSIX prototypes are requested per-file). Build a clean
  snapshot and drop it into your project:

    bmake dist                          # -> pxl-<commit>-<backend>.tar.gz
    bmake PXL_BACKEND=sdl dist          # SDL2 variant
    mkdir -p vendor/pxl
    tar -xzf pxl-<commit>-<backend>.tar.gz -C vendor/pxl --strip-components=1

  Then either compile the sources directly in your own build system:
    cc -std=c99 -Ivendor/pxl -c vendor/pxl/*.c
    cc ... *.o $(pkg-config --cflags --libs x11 xext)     # or: sdl2
  or build the static library with bmake: 'bmake -C vendor/pxl', link -lpxl.
  Note: Makefile.inc is bmake syntax; with another build system, use the
  pkg-config line above for the backend cflags/libs.
  The snapshot ships exactly one backend_*.c (PXL_BACKEND at dist time,
  default x11); copy the other backend file from the full repo to switch.
  Keep LICENSE inside vendor/pxl and record the upstream commit there
  (e.g. in vendor/pxl/VENDORED-AT) so updates stay traceable.
  When vendoring several flat C libraries side by side (pxl and rlk both
  ship err.h/geom.h), use a single include root and prefixed paths:
    cc -Ivendor ...    with #include "pxl/pxl.h"   /* never bare "err.h" */
  Quoted includes inside a header resolve in its own directory first, so
  umbrella headers stay unambiguous regardless of -I order.


Quick start (Minimal PXL application):
    pxl_app_t app = {
        .title = "My App",
        .width = 800,
        .height = 600
    };

    if (pxl_app_init(&app) != PXL_SUCCESS) return 1;

    while (pxl_app_advance_wait(&app)) {
        if (pxl_app_was_pressed(&app, PXL_KEYB_ESCAPE)) break;

        pxl_buf_t pb;
        if (pxl_backend_begin_frame(&pb) == PXL_SUCCESS) {
            pxl_canvas_t cnv;
            pxl_canvas_init(&cnv, &pb);
            pxl_canvas_clear(&cnv);

            pxl_draw_str(&cnv, 100, 100, "Hello, PXL!");

            (void)pxl_backend_end_frame();
        }
    }

    pxl_app_deinit(&app);


Demos:
  - demo_pong.c        - Complete game: physics, input, rendering, interpolation
  - demo_fontview.c    - Bitmask font viewer


Architecture:
  Core:
    backend.h      - Backend interface. All backends use ARGB8888 pixel format
    buf.h          - uint32_t pixel buffer with stride alignment
    err.h          - Error codes
    geom.h         - Geometry primitives (rect, span) and clipping
    input.h        - Input state handling (keyboard, mouse, window events)

  Backend:
    backend_sdl.c - SDL2 backend (do not activate VSYNC)
    backend_x11.c - X11 backend (uses SHM, XIC extensions for performance)

  Gfx:
    bitmask.h      - 1-bit per pixel mask for stencil/clip operations
    blit.h/c       - Pixel operations (blit, bitmask drawing, with optional flip/scale)
    canvas.h       - Drawing surface with color, scissor, translation offset, clear, blit
    color.h        - ARGB8888 color creation and component extraction
    shape.h/c      - 2D primitives (line, rect, circle, triangle, outline + filled)
    text.h/c       - Text rendering with mono or proportional LSB bitmask fonts, alignment, and transformations
    text_basic.h/c - ASCII text rendering with built-in 8x8 font (char, string, bounds)

  Framework:
    app.h          - App management: frame management, input, poll/wait event modes
    layout.h       - Layout helpers
    stepper.h      - Time-stepped physics loop helper (fixed timestep, interpolation)

  Deprecated (will be removed in next version):
    camera.h       - Offset-based camera management helpers (use canvas offset directly)
    tileset.h/c    - Tile rendering: grid atlas (tileset) + animation frames (sprite) (use pxl_blit_rect directly)
    timer.h        - Countdown timer helpers (use a double variable directly)


  pxl.h - umbrella header that includes all public headers. For finer
          granularity, users may include individual headers directly.

Tools:
  - bdf2pxl - Convert BDF font files to pxl_font_t C header
    Example: bdf2pxl -n my_font -r U+0020-U+007F DejaVuSans.bdf > my_font.h


Testing:
  Run tests: 'make test', or 'make check' for the full suite (lint + tests +
  demos, both x11 and sdl backends, tools) via check.sh.


